    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d262-f1" n="8" xml:id="d262-f1-content">
                <p>According to American records, the following additional officials were present on
                    the American side: Assistant Secretary of State Dunn; Lt. Gen. Lucius D. Clay,
                    United States Military Governor in Germany; Robert D. Murphy, United States
                    Political Adviser for Germany; and Edwin W. Pauley, President Truman’s personal
                    representative on reparations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
